  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers W3C WAI-ARIA 1.2 (Recommendation 2023-06-06) for authors and reviewers of accessible web components: role categories and abstract roles, required owned elements, context roles and required states, supported and prohibited attributes, hiding and live regions; accessible name and description computation per AccName; the ARIA in HTML author requirements and the rules of ARIA use; and the APG keyboard and focus patterns for modal dialog, alert dialog, menu button, menu and menubar, combobox, listbox, tabs, disclosure, grid, tree view and alerts. Version lines: WAI-ARIA 1.2 is current, 1.1 and 1.0 are legacy upgrade input, and the 1.3 Working Draft is a preview with posture name; AccName 1.1 is the current AccName Recommendation and AccName 1.2 a preview with posture build; ARIA in HTML (Recommendation 2026-08-11) is current. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines, roles, states and properties, accessible names, ARIA in HTML, and the APG patterns.",
